# Environment: airlock sandbox

You are running inside **airlock**, an isolated container made for this project.
This file is generated at every start; do not edit it.

## Where you are

- The project is at `{{.ProjectDir}}`: the same path as on the user's computer.
  It is shared with the host, so everything you write there appears on the
  user's machine. Everything outside the project and the mounts below is the
  container's own filesystem.
- The container is {{if .Persistent}}persistent: tools you install stay when it is stopped and started again, and are lost only when the user removes it (`airlock rm`){{else}}ephemeral: it is thrown away when it stops. Anything outside the project and the mounts below is lost{{end}}.
- You have passwordless `sudo` inside the container only. Docker is not available inside it.

